cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Zoe.Logos-Graph: A comparative atlas of animal vocal communication"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Antonella Maria Cristina"
    family-names: "Torrisi"
    email: a.m.c.torrisi@qmul.ac.uk
    affiliation: "Centre for Digital Music, Queen Mary University of London"
repository-code: "https://github.com/antorr91/Zoe.Logos-Graph"
url: "https://antorr91.github.io/Zoe.Logos-Graph/"
abstract: >
  Zoe.Logos-Graph is an open, interactive knowledge resource that
  integrates more than 750 species, peer-reviewed studies updated
  every two weeks, and openly licensed recordings into a navigable
  knowledge graph of animal communication. It supports cross-species
  comparison across seven zoological classes and 16 research themes, including vocal
  learning, referential signalling, syntax, dialects, and
  communicative function. Community detection on a weighted
  species-trait projection reveals emergent clusters of functionally
  similar species. Audio comes from Xeno-Canto, iNaturalist and GBIF.
keywords:
  - bioacoustics
  - animal communication
  - knowledge graph
  - comparative cognition
  - vocal learning
  - zoosemiotics
  - open science
